0..70 Comment "// A function written as `fn (q) { e }` acts on a path through `cong`."
71..73 Comment "//"
74..148 Comment "// Whiskering composes each path of a path of paths with a fixed path. The"
149..221 Comment "// function that does it is short, and a stated type for it only repeats"
222..241 Comment "// the path\'s type."
242..244 Comment "//"
245..317 Comment "// The binder takes the type of the path\'s points. Where no path type is"
318..381 Comment "// stated, `cong` reads its own off the path type the body has."
382..384 Comment "//"
385..450 Comment "// - see: #3773 — a lambda as `cong`\'s function, refused before"
451..524 Comment "// - see: #3829 — a lambda where no path type is stated, refused before"
